be here until midnight," Will said. "And I have no idea how to score these dancers.

32
00:03:19.707 --> 00:03:28.222
Charlie obviously scores low in the coordination category, but aside from that . . ." "It's

33
00:03:28.223 --> 00:03:33.203
harder than I thought it would be, but we can do this," Javier said. "Why don't

34
00:03:33.204 --> 00:03:38.796
you take over demonstrating the steps? I'll help Mr. D. with the judging." The afternoon wore on.

35
00:03:38.797 --> 00:03:46.694
One kid kept looking at his feet. Javier gave him a zero in the confidence and

36
00:03:46.695 --> 00:03:54.862
attitude category. Another dancer kept talking to his friend. Eventually the two of them stopped trying

37
00:03:54.863 --> 00:03:58.100
to keep up and sat on the bleachers. Javier rated them low on energy. But then

38
00:03:58.101 --> 00:04:09.010
there were the kids who could really dance. One was amazing at freestyling and big moves

39
00:04:09.011 --> 00:04:13.247
like head spins and flares. "He's even better than Malcolm!" Javier said excitedly. When Will demonstrated

40
00:04:13.248 --> 00:04:23.081
some complicated choreography, one kid caught on right away. Another kid was really good at synchronizing

41
00:04:23.082 --> 00:04:31.415
his movements to the beat. "I like him," said Mr. D., who'd been tapping his fingers

42
00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:40.648
to the music. There were also kids who understood that they were all supposed to be

43
00:04:40.649 --> 00:04:45.885
moving as one unit. But by the end of the afternoon, there was still a big

44
00:04:45.886 --> 00:04:50.067
problem. "We have some talented guys here." Will looked over the scores. "But nobody has all

45
00:04:50.068 --> 00:04:58.073
the skills we need." "Maybe we should have another day of auditions?" Javier suggested. "We need

46
00:04:58.074 --> 00:05:02.136
the best guys to get on the show. What do you think, Mr. D.?" "It's up

47
00:05:02.137 --> 00:05:06.877
to you two to decide." Javier's phone buzzed. It was Today's Tryout Tip: A unifying look

48
00:05:06.878 --> 00:05:09.210
for your group makes a good impression on the judges. Javier had no idea what their

49
00:05:09.211 --> 00:05:18.872
crew's look was, never mind if it was unified. But he was suddenly sure of one

50
00:05:18.873 --> 00:05:26.356
thing. "No more auditions. We need to decide today because we have a lot of work

51
00:05:26.357 --> 00:05:32.020
to do." So Javier and Will chose three guys—Pablo, the freestyler with all the big moves;

52
00:05:32.021 --> 00:05:43.838
Christopher, whose footwork was amazing; and Harry, who paid close attention to the beat. *** Tessa

53
00:05:43.839 --> 00:05:52.257
pounced on Javier as soon as he came upstairs. "How did it go? Did anybody show

54
00:05:52.258 --> 00:05:55.234
up to the audition?" "Oh yeah, way too many guys." Tessa followed him to his room.

55
00:05:55.235 --> 00:06:02.095
"Are you holding another audition?" "No, it was pretty easy to find the best dancers." Javier

56
00:06:02.096 --> 00:06:08.404
tried to sound confident with Tessa. He didn't want to get into a discussion with her.

57
00:06:08.405 --> 00:06:16.156
Not now—when he was already overwhelmed by all this dance crew stuff. "Besides, we don't have

58
00:06:16.157 --> 00:06:23.657
time for more auditions," he added. " Best American Talent is coming to town in two

59
00:06:23.658 --> 00:06:29.308
months." "That's no time at all!" "We'll get lots of practice at basketball games." Tessa looked

60
00:06:29.309 --> 00:06:33.636
skeptical. "When does basketball season start?" "Two weeks." "Two weeks?" Tessa squeaked. "Are you serious? Have

61
00:06:33.637 --> 00:06:40.976
you picked your music yet?" "Well, sort of." Javier thought about the music they used to

62
00:06:40.977 --> 00:06:51.051
dance to—Malcolm's favorites. He hated Malcolm's taste in music. They should definitely throw everything out and

63
00:06:51.052 --> 00:06:56.884
start again, but that would require even more time. "Do you know what you're going to

64
